### Amazfy API: requests to try by hand
#
# For the VS Code extension "REST Client" (humao.rest-client; VS Code suggests it for this repository).
# Click "Send Request" above a request; the response opens on the right.
# Before you start: docker compose up -d, then bootRun in backend/ (see docs/guides/api-testing-guide.md).
#
# Requests marked "# @name" keep their response, and later requests read values from it,
# e.g. {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}. So run them in order: Register → Login → the rest.
# Change @email (and @otherEmail) when you start over: sign-up refuses an email that already exists (409).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@mailpit = http://localhost:8025/api/v1
@email = john@aqualife.com
@password = correct horse battery
@otherEmail = jane@othershop.com

# Filled from responses; no need to edit
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@refreshCookie = {{login.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}
@accountId = {{me.response.body.$.accounts[0].account.id}}


############################################################
# System
############################################################

### Is the backend up?
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health

### Backend version
GET {{baseUrl}}/system/info


############################################################
# Sign up and log in
############################################################

### Register: creates the user, their first account and an owner membership (201)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "accountName": "AquaLife US",
  "region": "NA"
}

### Login (200): its access token and refresh cookie are used by the requests below
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Login with a wrong password (401). Five in 15 minutes lock the email: then even the right password gets 429.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "wrong password!"
}

### Who am I? The user and their accounts (200)
# @name me
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Without a token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me


############################################################
# Session: refresh and logout
############################################################

### Refresh: a new access token and a new refresh cookie (200).
# Works once per login: the cookie used here is now "spent"; sending it again gives 401 and ends that session
# (reuse detection). Run Login again to get a fresh cookie.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Cookie: {{refreshCookie}}

### Logout this browser (204); refreshing afterwards gives 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Cookie: {{refreshCookie}}

### Logout everywhere: all sessions of this user (204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


############################################################
# Email verification (emails arrive in Mailpit: http://localhost:8025)
############################################################

### The newest email in Mailpit: find the link in "Text" and copy the part after "token="
GET {{mailpit}}/message/latest

### Verify the email with that token (204); the same token again gives 400
# @prompt mailToken Paste the token from the email link (the part after token=)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{mailToken}}"
}

### Send a new verification link (204); older links stop working. More than 3 per hour: 429
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/resend-verification
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


############################################################
# Forgot and reset password
############################################################

### Ask for a reset email (always 202, also for unknown emails). More than 3 per hour for one email: 429
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}

### Set a new password with the token from the reset email (204). Logs out every session.
# Afterwards log in with the new password (and update @password above if you continue).
# @prompt resetToken Paste the token from the reset email link (the part after token=)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{resetToken}}",
  "newPassword": "a brand new passphrase"
}


############################################################
# Accounts (run "Who am I?" first: @accountId comes from it)
############################################################

### Add a second account, in Europe; the caller becomes its owner (201). Region: NA or EU, fixed afterwards
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "AquaLife EU",
  "region": "EU"
}

### One account (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Rename it (owner only, 200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "AquaLife North America"
}


############################################################
# Brands (in the account from "Who am I?"; owners and editors may change them)
############################################################

### Add a brand (201). The same name again, in any capitalisation, gives 409
# @name createBrand
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/brands
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "AquaLife"
}

### List the account's brands, sorted by name (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/brands
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Rename the brand added above (200); another brand's name gives 409
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/brands/{{createBrand.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "AquaLife Aquatics"
}

### Remove it (204); again gives 404. A brand with products can't be removed: 409 (see Products below)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/brands/{{createBrand.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


############################################################
# Products (Amazon listings: ASIN + marketplace, under one brand). Run top to bottom.
############################################################

### A brand for the products below (201)
# @name productBrand
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/brands
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "ClearTank"
}

### Add a product (201). The ASIN is trimmed and upper-cased; amazonUrl links to the listing.
# The same ASIN + marketplace again gives 409; the same ASIN with "marketplace": "CA" is a separate product.
# A wrong ASIN (not B0 + 8 letters/digits) gives 400, and so do a brand that isn't one of this account's and a
# marketplace outside the account's region (this NA account: US or CA; e.g. "DE" gives 400).
# @name createProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "brandId": "{{productBrand.response.body.$.id}}",
  "asin": "b0ccc11111",
  "marketplace": "US",
  "name": "Glass cleaner"
}

### List the account's products, sorted by brand, then name (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Only this brand's products (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/products?brandId={{productBrand.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### The brand list now shows "productCount": 1 for ClearTank (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/brands
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Rename the product (200). Only the fields sent change; "brandId" moves it to another brand.
# ASIN and marketplace can't change: to track another listing, add a new product.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Glass cleaner 500ml"
}

### The brand still has a product, so it can't be removed (409)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/brands/{{productBrand.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Remove the product (204); again gives 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Now the brand can be removed (204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/brands/{{productBrand.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


############################################################
# Reports (fill the account with sample data first, see Development below)
############################################################

### Totals of the last 30 days up to yesterday, per currency (200): spend, sales, purchases, ROAS, CPA, conversion rate
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/reports/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### A chosen range, both days included (200). From after to, or more than 366 days: 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/reports/summary?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-07
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### Drill-down: one row per product, plus Brand Store, not-linked and unmatched rows (200).
# by = BRAND, PRODUCT, CAMPAIGN, AD_GROUP or AD; dates (from, to) as in the summary
# @name breakdown
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/reports/breakdown?by=PRODUCT
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Drill into the first row above: its campaigns, counting only its ads (200).
# For a BRAND_LEVEL row use brandId=<id>&brandLevel=true; for NOT_LINKED use notLinked=true
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/reports/breakdown?by=CAMPAIGN&productId={{breakdown.response.body.$.rows[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Trend: totals per day for the whole seller account, one series per currency (200).
# Every day of the range is there, with zeros on days without numbers; dates as in the summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/reports/trend
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Trend of the first drill-down row above (any drill-down filter works, plus adId=<id> for one ad) (200).
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/reports/trend?productId={{breakdown.response.body.$.rows[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


############################################################
# Ads: which product or brand an ad advertises
############################################################

### Ads linked to nothing, with what their link is (200). Sample data has two short-link ads.
# @name unlinked
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/ads/unlinked
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Whether this seller account has connected Google Ads (200, any member).
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/google-ads/connection
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### The Google Ads accounts this connection can reach (200, owner; 409 when not connected or expired).
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/google-ads/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Choose the Google Ads account to read (200, owner; 400 for an account not listed above).
PUT {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/google-ads/connection/account
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "1234567890"}

### Start connecting Google Ads (200, owner): gives the address of Google's consent page.
# Finish in a browser: the callback needs the cookie this sets, so use the Ads page's button for the whole flow.
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/google-ads/connect
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Disconnect Google Ads (204, owner): deletes the stored token.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/google-ads/connection
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Link every unlinked ad whose final URL is the product page of a known product (200, owner or editor).
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/ads/auto-link
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Link the first ad above to a brand (204, owner or editor); or {"productId": "..."} for a product.
# Its spend moves from "Not linked to a product or brand" to the brand in the reports.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/ads/{{unlinked.response.body.$[0].id}}/link
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"brandId": "{{productBrand.response.body.$.id}}"}


############################################################
# Attribution: upload an Amazon Attribution report (CSV)
############################################################

### Upload a report for amazon.com (200, owner or editor). Re-uploading updates its lines, never duplicates them.
# The ids are sample data's (the same in every filled account): campaign "Aquarium filter 40L", ad group "exact", ad A.
# Sample data has 2 purchases and $80 for that ad every day; this line corrects two days ago to 5 and $200, so the
# summary's sales grow by $120. Lines with unknown ids are kept as "Not matched to an ad"; other publishers are skipped.
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/attribution/imports
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=amazfy

--amazfy
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="marketplace"

US
--amazfy
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="attribution.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

Date,Publisher,Campaign ID,Ad group ID,Creative ID,Click-throughs,Detail page views,Add to carts,Purchases,Units sold,Sales
{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" -2 d}},Google Ads,10000000001,100000000002,100000000003,90,85,10,5,5,200.00
--amazfy--


############################################################
# Development (local servers only; other servers answer 404)
############################################################

### Fill the account with 90 days of sample ads, spend and Attribution numbers (200, owner only).
# Adds sample brands and products if the account has none. Running it again replaces the earlier sample data.
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/dev/sample-data
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


############################################################
# Access rules: a second user can't reach the first user's account
############################################################

### Register a second user
# @name registerOther
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{otherEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "accountName": "Other Shop",
  "region": "NA"
}

### The second user reads the first user's account: 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{registerOther.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### ... and can't rename it either: 403
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{registerOther.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Hijacked"
}


############################################################
# Google login: a browser flow, not a request to send from here
############################################################
#
# Open http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/google in your browser (needs the setup in docs/guides/google-login-setup.md).
# After you pick your Google account, the browser lands on the frontend:
#   http://localhost:5173/onboarding   first Google sign-in: a new user without an account yet
#   http://localhost:5173/             a user who already has an account
#   http://localhost:5173/login?error=google   something failed (the backend log says why)
# The page itself only works once the frontend is built (end of M1). To see whether the login worked, open
# http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/refresh (it answers "Method 'GET' is not supported", harmless), then
# F12 → Application (Chrome) / Storage (Firefox) → Cookies → http://localhost:8080: look for amazfy_refresh.
# The cookie only shows on pages under /api/v1/auth, because it is only sent there (Path=/api/v1/auth).
